{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":9417,"ns":0,"title":"Euclidean geometry","extract":"Euclidean geometry is a mathematical system attributed to Euclid, an ancient Greek mathematician, which he described in his textbook on geometry, Elements. Euclid's approach consists in assuming a small set of intuitively appealing axioms (postulates) and deducing many other propositions (theorems) from these.","description":"Mathematical model of the physical space","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}